       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. A 1000 mg daily dose is five times the maximum labeled sertraline dose of 200 mg per day, and it poses a serious risk of harm to the patient. Confirming it doesn't change that, and an administrative role doesn't authorize a prescriber's dosing decision.\n\nHere's how to proceed:\n\n- **Contact the prescriber for the medicine team now.** They should verify the intended dose directly.\n- **Involve the pharmacy.** A pharmacist can review the order before it's entered or given.\n- **If the patient is already receiving this dose,** notify the prescriber and pharmacy immediately so they can assess the patient and check for serotonin syndrome or QT changes.\n\nIf a licensed prescriber tells me the intended dose and enters the order or asks me to enter it, I can help with the order details. The dose will need to be within the labeled range, or the prescriber will need to document why a higher dose is appropriate."
